{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">The problem</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A table may render one row template many times. Every row needs its own DOM ID so HTMX can replace exactly that row, while the parent still uses native Go template composition.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;table&gt;
{{ "{{ range .Rows }}" }}
    {{ "{{ template \"user_row.gohtml\" . }}" }}
{{ "{{ end }}" }}
&lt;/table&gt;</code></pre>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;tr id="row-{{ "{{ .ID }}" }}"&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;{{ "{{ .Name }}" }}&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;
        &lt;button hx-post="/users/{{ "{{ .ID }}" }}/refresh"
                hx-target="#row-{{ "{{ .ID }}" }}"
                hx-swap="outerHTML"&gt;Refresh&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Wire the resolver</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The connector reads the requested target from the request. For HTMX this is <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Target</code>. If the target is not a registered region ID, go-partial asks the resolver whether it can map that target to a partial and fresh dot value. The resolver runs in <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">target.Stage()</code>, which must be in use, and is looked up on the partial passed to <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Write</code> and its ancestors.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">rowPartial := partial.NewID("row", "templates/users/user_row.gohtml")

table := partial.NewID("content", "templates/users/table.gohtml").
    SetDot(UserTablePage{Rows: rows}).
    With(rowPartial).
    Use(target.Stage())

target.WithResolver(table, func(ctx context.Context, r *http.Request, target string) (*partial.Partial, bool) {
    if !strings.HasPrefix(target, "row-") {
        return nil, false
    }

    id, err := strconv.Atoi(strings.TrimPrefix(target, "row-"))
    if err != nil {
        return nil, false
    }

    row, ok := loadUserRow(ctx, id)
    if !ok {
        return nil, false
    }

    return partial.NewID(target, "templates/users/user_row.gohtml").SetDot(row), true
})</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Request flow</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>The browser sends an HTMX request with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Target: row-42</code>.</li>
        <li>The connector marks it as a partial request and exposes the target value.</li>
        <li>go-partial first checks for a registered region with ID <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">row-42</code>.</li>
        <li>If no registered region exists, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">target.WithResolver</code> receives <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">row-42</code>.</li>
        <li>The resolver returns the row template partial with fresh dot data for row 42.</li>
        <li>The row template is rendered, followed by the out-of-band regions of the partial that resolved it and of its ancestors, and swapped into <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">#row-42</code>.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Rules of thumb</h2>
    <ul class="docs-list list-disc">
        <li>Keep DOM IDs stable and unique, such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">row-{{ "{" }}id{{ "}" }}</code>.</li>
        <li>Do not cache row HTML when row data can change. Resolve fresh data per request.</li>
        <li>Return <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">false</code> for unknown target shapes, so the target fallback or the usual error answers them.</li>
        <li>Use native <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">template</code> calls for repeated rendering, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">target.WithResolver</code> for targeted replacement of one repeated item.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Regions of resolved targets</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A resolved partial gets the out-of-band regions of the partial that resolved it and of its parents, as a registered child does. A target an earlier stage resolved is left as it is.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Fragments and regions with slots</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/slots</code> covers two common targets without a resolver. A region is placed on the page with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ slot \"cart\" }}" }}</code> and sent out of band with every partial response; a fragment is answered on its own when a request targets its ID and the page can render it, else left to the target fallback. Slots are looked up through the ancestors, so a content template can place a slot of the layout.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.Use(slots.Stage())
slots.Set(root, "cart", cart, slots.OOB())
slots.Set(root, "comments", comments, slots.CheckContracts(), slots.OmitOOB())</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">CheckContracts</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">OmitOOB</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Deferred</code> make a slot standalone: the stage answers requests for its ID. A slot without options is registered as a child of the partial it is set on. Out-of-band regions go in the order they were registered, nearest partial first, so the same page gives the same bytes on every render.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Deferred, globbed and required slots</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A deferred slot loads after the page: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ slot }}" }}</code> renders a placeholder that requests the slot from the page's address through the connector, and the request renders the slot alone, with its lazy dot. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">slots.Placeholder(p)</code> renders a placeholder of the application's own with a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">slots.PlaceholderData</code> dot, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">slots.Data(v)</code> gives that dot data of the slot's own. See <a href="{{ basePath }}/deferred" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/deferred" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">Deferred partials</a>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">slots.Set(root, "recent", recent.SetDotSource(partial.DotFuncOf(loadRecent)), slots.Deferred(), slots.OmitOOB())</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">slots.Glob</code> sets a slot for every file of a directory, named after the file (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">menu</code> for <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">regions/menu.gohtml</code>), and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">slots.Setup</code> configures each slot's partial. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ requiredSlot \"name\" }}" }}</code> fails the template for a slot that is not set; <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ hasSlot \"name\" }}" }}</code> checks optional ones. The template that places a slot can defer it itself with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ deferredSlot \"popular\" \"reveal\" }}" }}</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">err := slots.Glob(root, "regions/*.gohtml", slots.OOB(), slots.Setup(func(name string, region *partial.Partial) {
    region.SetDot(view)
}))</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Sending only some elements of a region</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetOOBElements(ids...)</code> makes a region that goes out of band send only the elements of its output with those IDs, each with the connector's out-of-band attribute, such as the items of a menu that mark the page being shown. When none of the IDs is in the output, the whole region goes; on a full page the region renders whole. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetOOBElementsFunc(fn)</code> chooses the IDs per request and names the request headers they depend on for <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Vary</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">menu := partial.NewID("menu", "templates/menu.gohtml").SetOOBElements("menu-about", "menu-contact")

menu.SetOOBElementsFunc(func(r *http.Request) partial.OOBElements {
    return partial.OOBElements{
        IDs:  changedItems(connector.CurrentURL(conn, r), r.URL),
        Vary: []string{connector.CurrentURLHeader(conn)},
    }
})</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">A region in the head</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A region placed in <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">&lt;head&gt;</code>, with the page's canonical, alternate and feed links, description or structured data, cannot go out of band as other regions do: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">&lt;head&gt;</code> holds no element to wrap it, and the number of its elements changes from page to page. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">head.Region(p)</code> of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/head</code> makes a partial such a region. On a full page its output sits between two empty <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">&lt;template&gt;</code> markers (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">head.StartAttr</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">head.EndAttr</code>); out of band it replaces whatever is between them, as a group.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">region := head.Region(partial.NewID("head", "regions/head.gohtml").SetDot(page))
slots.Set(root, "head", region, slots.OOB())

&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset="utf-8"&gt;
    {{ "{{ slot \"head\" }}" }}
&lt;/head&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">With htmx 2 and 4 the region goes as two out-of-band swaps that need no extension: a delete of the elements between the markers and an insert before the end marker. A <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">&lt;title&gt;</code> in the region's output goes on its own, where htmx sets the document's title from it. The region needs no ID and no <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ oobAttr }}" }}</code>. With a connector whose out-of-band attribute is not <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-swap-oob</code>, such as Unpoly's, the output goes as it is.</p>
</article>


